reasoning:
We need to analyze the problem.

The test scenario:

Journey steps:
1. Seek #store (focus)
2. Type "ma"
3. Press ArrowDown -> expects aria-selected true on #autoCompleteJS_result_0 and aria-activedescendant on #store equals "autoCompleteJS_result_0".
But observed: After pressing ArrowDown, we got aria-activedescendant="Market Street", which is wrong because expected was "autoCompleteJS_result_0".

Observation: In the observed step details, after typing "ma", the input had aria-activedescendant already set to "Market Street"? Let's look at the observed before/after states.

In failed step index 2 (the first ArrowDown press):
Before: input html shows no aria-activedescendant attribute present? Actually before: `<input ...>` ends with just closing bracket, no aria-activedescendant attribute. So initially none.

After: input html includes `aria-activedescendant="Market Street"` . That suggests that after the first ArrowDown, the script incorrectly set aria-activedescendant to the text content of the first suggestion ("Market Street") rather than the ID of the element.

Thus the bug likely lies in navigation controller's update function where it sets aria-activedescendant using list[currentFocus].dataset.value instead of the element's id.

Let's examine navigationController.js snippet provided.

From given source:

```
const update = (event, list, state, config) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    if (state) {
      // If the arrow DOWN or TAB key is pressed
      // increase the currentFocus
      currentFocus++;
    } else {
      // If the arrow UP or TAB key is pressed
      // decrease the currentFocus
      currentFocus--;
    }
    // and add "active" class to the list item
    addActive(list);
    config.inputField.setAttribute("aria-activedescendant", list[currentFocus].dataset.value);
```

So indeed they use dataset.value (which presumably holds the value string like "Market Street").

But what should be used? According to ARIA spec, aria-activedescendant should refer to the ID of the active descendant element (the option). The list items have IDs generated by Item.js: result.setAttribute("id", `${config.resultItem.className}_${index}`); Also they set data-value attribute to item.value[item.key].

Thus we need to set aria-activedescendant to the element's id, not its data-value.

Therefore edit navigationController.js line setting aria-activedescendant to use list[currentFocus].id.

Check also other places: maybe also in removeActive etc but fine.

Now verify that the list items have id set correctly: In Item.js: result.setAttribute("id", `${config.resultItem.className}_${index}`); And className is "autoCompleteJS_result". So id would be like "autoCompleteJS_result_0". Good.

Thus editing navigationController.js accordingly.

Now ensure we don't break anything else: The dataset.value may still be used elsewhere? Not needed.

Potential side effects: The navigation controller also uses list[currentFocus].dataset.value maybe elsewhere? Only seen in that line. We'll replace.

Now produce the edit.

We need to provide before and after strings: minimal region around that line.

Let's extract the relevant part from navigationController.js source:

Full source:

```
import { closeAllLists } from "./listController";
import eventEmitter from "../utils/eventEmitter";

/**
 * List navigation function initializer
 *
 * @param {Object} config - autoCompleteJS configurations
 *
 */
const navigate = (config, results, dataFeedback) => {
  // Reset focus state
  let currentFocus = -1;

  /**
   * Update list item state
   *
   * @param {Object} event - The `keydown` event Object
   * @param {Array <elements>} list - The array of list items
   * @param {Object} config - autoCompleteJS configurations
   *
   */
  const update = (event, list, state, config) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    if (state) {
      // If the arrow DOWN or TAB key is pressed
      // increase the currentFocus
      currentFocus++;
    } else {
      // If the arrow UP or TAB key is pressed
      // decrease the currentFocus
      currentFocus--;
    }
    // and add "active" class to the list item
    addActive(list);
    config.inputField.setAttribute("aria-activedescendant", list[currentFocus].dataset.value);
    /**
     * @emits {navigation} Emits Event on results list navigation
     **/
    eventEmitter(
      event.srcElement,
      { event, ...dataFeedback, matches: results, selection: results[currentFocus] },
      "navigation"
    );
  };

  /**
   * Remove list item active state
   *
   * @param {Array <elements>} list - The array of list items
   *
   */
  const removeActive = (list) => {
    // Remove "active" class from all list items
    for (let index = 0; index < list.length; index++) {
      // Remove "active" class from the item
      list[index].removeAttribute("aria-selected");
      // list[index].setAttribute("aria-selected", "false");
      list[index].classList.remove("autoCompleteJS_selected");
    }
  };

  /**
   * Add active state to list item
   *
   * @param {Array <elements>} list - The array of list items
   *
   */
  const addActive = (list) => {
    // Add "active" class to a list item
    if (!list) return false;
    // Remove "active" class from all list items
    removeActive(list);
    if (currentFocus >= list.length) currentFocus = 0;
    if (currentFocus < 0) currentFocus = list.length - 1;
    // Add "active" class to the item
    list[currentFocus].setAttribute("aria-selected", "true");
    list[currentFocus].classList.add("autoCompleteJS_selected");
  };

  /**
   * List Navigation Function
   *
   * @param {Object} event - The `keydown` event Object
   *
   */
  const navigation = (event) => {
    let list = document.getElementById(config.resultsList.idName);

    if (!list) return config.inputField.removeEventListener("keydown", navigate);

    list = list.getElementsByTagName(config.resultItem.element);

    if (event.keyCode === 27) {
      // If the ESC key is pressed
      // Clear Input value
      config.inputField.value = "";
      // Closes open lists
      closeAllLists(false, event.target);
    } else if (event.keyCode === 40 || event.keyCode === 9) {
      // Update list items state
      update(event, list, true, config);
    } else if (event.keyCode === 38 || event.keyCode === 9) {
      // Update list items state
      update(event, list, false, config);
    } else if (event.keyCode === 13) {
      // If the ENTER key is pressed
      // prevent the form from its default behaviour "being submitted"
      event.preventDefault();
      if (currentFocus > -1) {
        // and simulate a click on the selected "active" item
        if (list) list[currentFocus].click();
      }
    }
  };

  const navigate = config.resultsList.navigation || navigation;
  /**
   * @listens {keydown} Listens to all `keydown` events on the input field
   **/
  config.inputField.addEventListener("keydown", navigate);
};

export { navigate };
```

We need to change line:

`config.inputField.setAttribute("aria-activedescendant", list[currentFocus].dataset.value);`

to

`config.inputField.setAttribute("aria-activedescendant", list[currentFocus].id);`

Make sure we keep same indentation.

