Root cause: The navigation controller incorrectly sets aria-activedescendant to the option's data-value (the label) instead of its ID, causing assistive technologies to announce the wrong active option.

Repair strategy: Change the assignment to use the option element's ID.

Expected accessibility effect: Arrow navigation will now correctly update aria-activedescendant to point to the active option element, allowing screen readers to announce the highlighted suggestion.

Functional risks: None significant; the change only affects the attribute value used for ARIA; the underlying selection and click behavior remain unchanged.

Verification requirements: Ensure that after typing "ma" and pressing ArrowDown, aria-activedescendant equals "autoCompleteJS_result_0"; after second ArrowDown equals "autoCompleteJS_result_1"; pressing Enter selects the highlighted option and fills the input with its value.

